1. Java is a high-level, object-oriented programming language.
2. Java follows the principle "Write Once, Run Anywhere (WORA)".
3. Java source code is stored in a .java file.
4. Java code is compiled into bytecode (.class file).
5. JVM (Java Virtual Machine) executes Java bytecode.
6. JDK contains JRE and development tools like the compiler.
7. JRE provides the environment to run Java programs.
8. Every Java program starts execution from the main() method.
9. Java is a case-sensitive language.
10. A class is the blueprint of an object.
11. An object is an instance of a class.
12. Variables are used to store data in memory.
13. Java has primitive and non-primitive data types.
14. Scanner class is used to take input from the user.
15. Operators perform operations on variables and values.
16. Conditional statements help in decision making.
17. Loops are used to execute a block of code repeatedly.
18. Methods improve code reusability and readability.
19. Arrays store multiple values of the same data type.
20. OOP concepts in Java are Encapsulation, Inheritance, Polymorphism, and Abstraction.
